Sun Oct 25 20:38:29 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to version 0.4.0:
  * Keep --format json stdout pure by running through a child
  * Support v6 OpenPGP signature entries
  * AlternativesCheck accepts exact-path libalternatives targets
  * SpecCheck gains licence-marking findings
  * Discover rpmlintrc beside every positional argument
  * Demote unused-rpmlintrc-filter, spelling-error and
    undefined-non-weak-symbol to warnings; sunset invalid-soname
  * Many precision fixes cutting false positives across Files,
    Binaries, Tags and Spec checks
  * Refresh vendored ctutils to 0.4.5, fixing RUSTSEC-2026-0385
    (no CVE assigned)
- Spec cleanup: sort Recommends after Requires

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Wed Oct 21 23:06:48 UTC 2026 - Tomáš Chvátal <tomas.chvatal@gmail.com>

- Require the data and tools the checks consume from the installed
  system, mirroring rpmlint and rpmlint-mini: polkit-default-privs
  on the rpmlint-compat subpackage (PolkitCheck reads the standard
  default-privs profile), file (magic classification via file -b),
  bash (scriptlet syntax checks via /bin/sh and /bin/bash -n) and
  the gzip, bzip2, xz and zstd decompressors (FilesCheck reads
  compressed files through the external tools); without them the
  affected checks silently degrade, in build roots substituting
  rpmcrab for rpmlint-mini as in plain installations. The en_US
  hunspell dictionary (myspell-en_US) is only recommended: the
  spell checker uses it when present and stays silent without it

