Tue Oct 20 15:21:44 UTC 2026 - Tomáš Chvátal <tomas.chvatal@gmail.com>

- Update to version 0.3.0
  * Signature verification runs in-process: signature packets are
    parsed with sequoia-openpgp and verified without invoking rpm,
    and malformed or unreadable signatures are reported instead of
    staying silent
  * Badness simplified: every error fails the build by default and
    the shipped configuration carries no badness values
  * The vendored distro configuration ships a single SUSE flavour
    (openSUSE); the SLFO flavour is removed
  * A weekly watch tracks upstream rpmlint configuration movement
    and files a tracking issue on drift; the vendored whitelist
    stanzas are synced from upstream
  * non-standard-uid/gid findings credit accounts the package
    itself declares and are promoted to errors; the
    file-contains-current-date findings are graded as errors
  * PAMModulesCheck is enabled in the bundled defaults and the
    openSUSE flavour, with the authorised module set derived from
    the FileDigestGroup data
  * Undefined symbols are resolved against the invocation package
    set, and x86_64 binaries missing control-flow protection are
    flagged
  * New scriptlet checks flag direct useradd and groupadd calls,
    daemon activation and deprecated cache updaters
- Drop the slfo.toml configuration file together with the SLFO
  flavour
- Re-vendor the cargo dependencies for the release (370 crates;
  adds sequoia-openpgp with its RustCrypto backend)
  * The package now uses the upstream release tarball as its source

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Sun Oct 18 21:18:40 UTC 2026 - Tomáš Chvátal <tomas.chvatal@gmail.com>

- Update to git snapshot 8381b07a (2026-10-18)
  * AtomicUpdateCheck is enabled in the bundled defaults and in
    the openSUSE and SLFO flavours
  * AtomicUpdateCheck warns on scriptlet writes outside the
    snapshot and on direct service restarts in scriptlets
  * Badness simplified: errors fail the build by default and the
    shipped configuration carries no badness values
  * bzip2-compressed payloads and source archives are decoded
  * New warning for %config-marked files below /usr/etc
  * file-digest XML validation hardened; systemd unit aliases are
    resolved before their targets are checked
- Re-vendor the cargo dependencies for the new snapshot (adds the
  bzip2 crate and its sys crate)

